+**Verified:** both test suites pass (20 + 7 OK); `import-city.sh` flags match `engine/cmd/netimport/main.go:22-27`; `scenario.yaml` fields match `engine/scenario/scenario.go:63-87` (`spawner.rate_per_lane_h` correct); render-city.py's lane fields (`internal`, `row`, `tl`, `speedLimit`, `shape`) match `engine/netfile.go:48-79`.
+
+**Contract check:** `contracts/network-format-v1.md` changes are recipe documentation only — no subject or payload schema change, no ADR required. Determinism: all script outputs are sorted or insertion-order deterministic; the `nxt.pop()` at scripts/osm-stop-nodes.py:329 is provably a singleton (`is_split` ⇒ exactly 2 ways, one already in `seen`), so no hash-order hazard.
+
+## Findings
+
+**Blockers:** none.
+
+**Should-fix**
+
+1. `scripts/osm-stop-nodes.py:259-271` — `incident_arms` counts every oneway way as 1 arm regardless of orientation. A oneway that *starts* at the junction (outbound-only; or ends there with `oneway=-1`) contributes zero real approaches but still inflates `total`, so `len(arms) >= total` can never be met and genuine all-way stops on one-way grids (common in SF, one of the six imports) get demoted to `priority_stop`. Fix is checking whether the junction sits at the way's exit end for oneways; a legit defer if the ep-03 renders looked right, but record it.
+
+**Nits**
+
+2. `scripts/osm-stop-nodes.py:297-298` — absent `direction` defaults to forward, a coin flip on two-way roads (can mark the junction *behind* the sign). A nearest-junction fallback would be more robust. Documented and tested as-is; fine to defer.
+3. `scripts/overpass2osm.py:483` — `_QUOTES` doesn't escape `\n`/`\t` in attribute values; XML parsers normalize them to spaces, harmless for netconvert, only matters if byte fidelity of tag values ever does.
+4. `scripts/test_overpass2osm.py:1026` — docstring says the golden was "captured from the pre-change script," but `overpass2osm.py` is new in this diff. Presumably the previously-untracked ep-03 copy; wording only, but a reader diffing history will be confused.
+5. `scripts/import-city.sh:82` — hardcoded `python3.12` venv path; consistent with the contract doc's recipe and the `-x` check at line 83 fails loudly, so acceptable.
+
+**Questions**
+
+6. `scripts/import-city.sh:92-113` — pass 2 relies on the base net's `<location>` element to carry `--proj.utm` forward; the comment documents the `--no-turnarounds` verification but not projection. Confirmed by the six-import verification? (Almost certainly yes — just confirm before recording.)
+7. `scripts/render-city.py:589-594` — matplotlib/numpy are new script-side dependencies. Conventions only govern Go/TS deps so no ADR is strictly required, but nothing states where they're expected to come from (the sumo venv?); a one-line note in the header would save the next person a guess.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
